<title>THAILAND: Union Bank to issue 100 mln new shares.</title>
<headline>Union Bank to issue 100 mln new shares.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Small-sized Union Bank of Bangkok Plc said on Friday that it would raise its registered capital to 1.8 billion baht ($72 million) from 800 million baht by issuing 100 million new shares.</p>
<p>The new shares would be offered to existing shareholders through a rights issue at the ratio of one old share to 1.25 new shares at 10 baht each, Union Bank said in a filing to the Stock Exchange of Thailand.</p>
</text>
